     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is a dose that can cause liver injury or liver failure. For a 70 kg patient it is near the supratherapeutic range of about 150 mg/kg (10.5 g) in 24 hours. I don't know of any indication that justifies it, and entering it could lead to real harm if it's verified and given.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours\n\nIf the order was meant to cover something unusual, such as an overdose protocol or a mix-up with another drug, tell me what you intended. A clinical pharmacist or toxicology consult is also an option."
      }
     ],
